Airflow emitted a `FutureWarning` ("Bad scheme ... You must change to `postgresql+psycopg`") for bare `postgresql://` metadata DB URLs. Those URLs are valid: Airflow only rewrites them to make the driver explicit (`postgresql+psycopg` if psycopg 3 is installed, otherwise `postgresql+psycopg2`). Users read the warning as "driver-less URLs are deprecated".

This change:
- stops warning for bare `postgresql://` (the rewrite itself is unchanged);
- keeps the warning for the actually unsupported `postgres://` and `postgres+psycopg2://` schemes, reworded to say what Airflow does and that `postgresql` (driver picked by Airflow) is a valid fix; the outdated SQLAlchemy 1.4 / Airflow 2.3 reference and the "before the next Airflow release" deadline are dropped;
- updates the `_upgrade_postgres_metastore_conn` docstring accordingly;
- adds a test that the warning is emitted only for `postgres` / `postgres+psycopg2`, and not for bare `postgresql`.

## Why

`@Airflow.*` makes it clear that they declare Airflow Dags and tasks.

## What

- Rename the annotation container `org.apache.airflow.sdk.Builder` to `org.apache.airflow.sdk.Airflow`.

```java
// Before
@Builder.Dag(id = "my_pipeline", schedule = "@daily")
public class MyPipeline {
  @Builder.Task(id = "extract", retries = 2)
  public long extract(Client client) { ... }

  @Builder.Deps
  static class Wiring implements MyPipelineDeps { ... }
}

// After
@Airflow.Dag(id = "my_pipeline", schedule = "@daily")
public class MyPipeline {
  @Airflow.Task(id = "extract", retries = 2)
  public long extract(Client client) { ... }

  @Airflow.Deps
  static class Wiring implements MyPipelineDeps { ... }
}
```

- The same rename applies to `@Airflow.If`, `@Airflow.Switch`, `@Airflow.TaskGroup` and `@Airflow.TaskHandler`.
- The generated `<Class>Builder` class and its `build()` method do not change.
- Rename `BuilderProcessor` to `AirflowProcessor`, and its test to match.
- Update the user docs, README, module docs, examples, e2e and k8s test bundles. ADRs are left as historical records.

