## Summary

Add `breeze ci-image environment-key`, an observational command that emits a versioned CI environment manifest and its SHA-256 fingerprint.

The fingerprint currently includes:

- the existing CI-image rebuild inputs;
- the root `uv.lock`;
- tracked `pyproject.toml` and `provider.yaml` files;
- the selected Python version and platform.

The CI workflow records this output as non-blocking telemetry.

## Deliberate limitations

This PR does **not** change CI-image construction or reuse:

- it does not build, select, or reuse an image;
- `reuse_eligible` is always `false`;
- base-image digests and all effective build parameters are not yet part of the fingerprint;
- an identical fingerprint must not be used to skip a build or skip tests;
- source, test, and untracked-file changes are not generally represented unless they affect one of the tracked environment inputs above.

The fingerprint is therefore provisional and diagnostic only. It is not a complete environment identity or a cache authorization mechanism.

## Relationship to follow-up work

This establishes the observational primitive for #74163. Future work must complete the environment identity, measure hit/miss behavior, validate cached-versus-current correctness, and preserve the existing build path as the fallback before enabling any reuse.

