## Why

Support the TaskFlow syntax to define the graph for native Dag with annotation syntax, follow the user interface design in [ADR-0002](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/java-sdk/adr/0002-native-dag-interface.md).

## Example

```java
@Builder.Dag(id = "java_etl", schedule = "@daily")
public class EtlPipeline {

  @Builder.Task(id = "extract", retries = 2)
  public long extract() { return 42L; }

  @Builder.Task(id = "transform")
  public long transform(long extracted, double factor) { return (long) (extracted * factor); }

  @Builder.Task(id = "audit")
  public void audit() { /* side effect only */ }

  @Builder.Deps
  static class Wiring implements EtlPipelineDeps {
    void depends() {
      var rows = extract();
      load(transform(rows, lit(0.9)));
      rows.before(audit()); // ordering-only edge
    }
  }
}
```

The processor generates the interface that wiring class implements:

```java
public interface EtlPipelineDeps extends Deps {
  default TaskRef<Long> extract() {
    return Refs.node(new TaskDef("extract", EtlPipelineBuilder.Extract.class).config("retries", 2));
  }

  default TaskRef<Long> transform(Arg<? extends Number> extracted, Arg<? extends Number> factor) {
    return Refs.call(new TaskDef("transform", EtlPipelineBuilder.Transform.class), extracted, factor);
  }
}
```

## How

- **A view, not a twin object.** The Dag class holds `long extract(Client)` while the view holds `TaskRef<Long> extract()` — two methods that would clash in one class. The wiring class *implements* the view, so the Dag class keeps its inheritance slot and, being `static`, cannot reach the real task methods.
- **Read by recording, not by parsing.** `depends()` runs once at registration with the Dag in scope. Nothing reads a syntax tree, so this works under any compiler rather than only javac.
- Passing a handle into another call wires a data edge and feeds the upstream's XCom into that parameter. `@Builder.Task` method must be called in the wiring class; a task the wiring missed fails at Dag-parse time.
- `Bundle.register(Class)` now also accepts a `@Builder.Dag` class and registers the Dag its generated builder builds.
- The task-level `.config(...)` assertion in `generateBuilderLowersConfigAttributes` moves from the builder golden into the wiring-view golden, because that is where the `TaskDef` is now constructed. It is relocated coverage, not lost coverage.

